From db2c87f9e845aad5584c105ab9cc9a4264b3d70e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elliotttate <elliotttate@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 20:40:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 128/128] gxcore: an ubershader draws what is still compiling

A draw whose pipeline was still compiling was left out of its frame: on a
new scene that is a few hundred draws a frame for the first frames, with
whole objects and walls popping in. As Dolphin's ubershaders do, a draw whose
own pipeline is not ready is now drawn with an ubershader: one WGSL module
(gxcore_uber.cpp) for any shader key, which it reads from its pixel uniform
(UberPixelConstants: the pixel constants, the key's bytes) and interprets -
lighting, texgens, the TEV stages, alpha test, fog - with a pipeline for each
fixed-function state (gxcore depthOnly 2) and a bind group of all eight
texmaps. Forced on every draw (DOL_AURORA_UBERSHADER=2) it draws the lava
rooms' frames identical to the specialized pipelines'.

Its pipelines for the states the cache's pipelines use are queued at start
(Dolphin's QueueUberSiblingStates). Its two shaders (plain, dual-source)
take about 650 ms each to compile when Dawn's blob cache does not have them;
from the cache a pipeline takes a few ms. So one pipeline per shader is made
before its others, and when depends on whether an earlier run made one (the
pipeline cache keeps the ubershader pipelines draws asked for): first if so,
otherwise only once the cache is queued and nothing else is.

Draws left out while their pipelines compiled (a batch now counts its
draws), booting into save states with the old 213-pipeline seed:
- a first launch (nothing in Dawn's cache): Gohma's room 5,933 against
  6,069 without the ubershader, Dragon Roost Cavern's lava room 5,296
  against 5,297, its bridge 4,613 against 4,848;
- after playing Outset once: 950 against 4,860, 141 against 3,477 and 215
  against 3,377 (3,910, 3,336 and 3,162 drawn with the ubershader).

DOL_AURORA_UBERSHADER=0 turns it off. The once-a-second report says how
many draws were left out and how many the ubershader drew.
